course: dictionary
lesson: 7028
title: A birth with no father
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Long science words are often made of smaller parts. Parthenogenesis comes from two Greek words: parthenos, meaning virgin or maiden, and genesis, meaning birth or beginning. Put them together and you can start to see the meaning.
explain: Most babies start when an egg joins with a sperm from a father. This joining is called fertilisation. In parthenogenesis, the egg starts to grow even though it was never fertilised, so no father is needed. «Female Komodo dragons in British zoos laid eggs that hatched with no father» is an example of this.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Female Komodo dragons in British zoos laid eggs that hatched with no father, a rare virgin birth called parthenogenesis.» The words "a rare virgin birth" are the author's own clue, so the meaning is a birth with no father.
fact: Parthenogenesis is a way of having babies from an egg that has not been fertilised, so no father is needed.
fact: Aphids, some lizards such as whiptail lizards, some sharks, Komodo dragons, water fleas and bees can all reproduce this way.
fact: Male honeybees, called drones, hatch from unfertilised eggs, so they have a mother but no father.
fact: The babies produced this way are often almost exact copies of their mother.
fact: Parthenogenesis is uncountable, so write "parthenogenesis", not "a parthenogenesis". You can say "reproduce by parthenogenesis".
exercise: «Female Komodo dragons in British zoos laid eggs that hatched with no father.» What is the name for this kind of birth? | Camouflage | *Parthenogenesis | Hibernation | Fertilisation
exercise: In parthenogenesis, is a father needed? | *No, the egg starts to grow without one | Yes, a father is always needed | Yes, but only for male babies
exercise: Which animal can reproduce by parthenogenesis? | *Aphid | Elephant | Tiger | Whale
test: The word parthenogenesis is made from the Greek words parthenos (virgin) and genesis. What does genesis mean? | Death | Father | Fertilised egg | *Birth or beginning
test: Which sentence uses parthenogenesis correctly? | The shark reproduced by parthenogenesis, so its babies had no father. | The parthenogenesis of the zoo was closed on Monday. | Parthenogenesis is a kind of food for lizards. | *Water fleas can reproduce by parthenogenesis, so the babies may have no father.
exam: Which statement about parthenogenesis is true? | Parthenogenesis always needs a male parent. | Parthenogenesis is only found in plants. | *Offspring from parthenogenesis are often almost copies of the mother. | Parthenogenesis means the egg joins with a sperm.
